Session: sub066 (lowest mean FD 0.0885; tmask keeps all 518 frames).
Each session is 518 timepoints × 630 parcels (616 cortical + 14
subcortical). TR = 1.16 s. The full 630-ROI covariance is rank 518
(T < p) and is therefore not published as a fixture.

Regenerated by `scripts/prep_myconnectome.py`.

  myconnectome/myconnectome_sub066_518x50.csv
    518 × 50. Network-balanced left-hemisphere subset listed in
    myconnectome/myconnectome_roi50.txt. Zero-network and subcortical
    parcels are excluded. Column names are P###_<network>_<hemi>.

  myconnectome/myconnectome_sub066_518x379.csv
    518 × 379, full rank (covariance rank 379, condition number
    ≈ 1.2×10^8). Deterministic network-stratified subset:
      1. Eligible = cortical parcels whose network is not Zero and
         whose lobe is not subcortical.
      2. Target n = 379 so T = 518 > p (open replacement for a
         non-redistributable HCP 520×379 Glasser series).
      3. Allocate slots to networks with the largest-remainder method,
         proportional to each network’s eligible count. Ties break
         by network name (ASCII).
      4. Inside a network, take the lowest parcel IDs.
    ROI list: myconnectome/myconnectome_roi379.txt
    sha256: myconnectome/myconnectome_sub066_518x379.sha256
    Parcel table: myconnectome/myconnectome_parcel_labels.csv
